        {
          "id": "krea2-92c31b1572e375ed1a53ebe8",
          "alias": "单女和服竹林行走",
          "prompt": "A woman wears a kimono with a pink base and intricate floral patterns. The kimono is adorned with purple-red chrysanthemums, pink and white cherry blossoms, pale purple hydrangeas, and green maple and bamboo leaf patterns. Black lace patterns are also decorated at the cuffs and hem, presenting the refined beauty of traditional Japanese kimono. Her makeup is fresh and natural. Facing the camera, she exudes a gentle and serene expression. Her right hand gently strokes the side of her neck, while her left hand hangs naturally in front of her. She held an off-white round handbag with metal fasteners on the body, giving it an elegant and vintage look. She stood on a street full of Japanese charm, with a typical Japanese machiya building in the background. On the wooden door frames and walls hung lanterns and cloth flags with Japanese signs such as \"Kashitsuka\" and \"Rabi-mochi.\" On the left, a white paper lantern hung on a bamboo pole, beside which was a pot of blooming yellow flowers. On the right, in the distance, you could see the backs of pedestrians and utility poles. The street was a dark gray stone pavement. The composition centers on the figure, using a mid-angle perspective where the figure occupies about two-thirds of the frame. The background is blurred to highlight the main subject, with natural light streaming in from the upper right side, creating natural shadows on the left side of the body, creating a warm and realistic light and shadow effect. The overall atmosphere is tranquil and full of life, as if capturing a moment of strolling through an old neighborhood in the afternoon. The tones are mainly pink, off-white, and pale yellow, complemented by green plants and a dark background for contrast. It presents an unintentional elegance and beauty found in everyday life. The image quality closely resembles real scenes shot with a regular phone, retaining slight noise and natural color transitions, and conveying a strong sense of life and documentary",
