        {
          "id": "krea2-b9e0b4991de2f98d9096e2d3",
          "alias": "单女米衬衫商店沉思站立注视",
          "prompt": "A woman stands inside a record store or secondhand bookstore filled with a retro atmosphere, her expression calm yet tinged with a hint of detachment. She wears a beige short-sleeved work shirt with a blue-gray plaid tie at the collar, black shorts, and a gray canvas bag slung across her waist with brown leather details. Her left hand rests casually on the black counter in front of her, while her right hand reaches toward the bookshelf on the right side of the painting. Her posture is relaxed yet elegant, and the overall look exudes an academic vibe that blends youth and art. In the foreground is a neat row of white bookshelves on the left, filled with various books and CD cases. Some of the cover patterns are blurry, and the edges show slight wear marks, showing the texture of use. There's also a small label labeled \"Live Shot\" on the shelf, adding a touch of everyday life. The center is the main figure, positioned slightly to the right of the center, her body slightly tilted but her head facing the camera, creating a strong visual focal point. The background features more stacked bookshelves and record racks. The top is densely packed with album covers and books. Some areas are blurred into soft light spots due to shallow depth of field, creating a sense of spatial depth. In the background, you can faintly see another customer's silhouette, adding a sense of authentic life to the scene. The composition uses the classic three-section layout, with figures near the golden ratio point. The left half of the frame is guided by a book structure, naturally drawing the viewer's gaze toward the main subject. The vertical lines of the foreground bookshelf contrast with the horizontal arrangement of the background shelves, enhancing the sense of structure in the image. It creates a strong emotional connection with the viewer, while the extended direction of the arm suggests she is browsing or selecting an object, guiding viewers to imagine her inner thoughts. In terms of lighting and shadow, the light source comes from the upper left of the frame, possibly the warm yellow spotlight inside the shop. The soft and directional lighting enhances the sense of depth. The overall color palette is mainly warm yellow and brown, creating a warm and nostalgic atmosphere. The lighting in the background casts soft halos on the bookshelves and walls, making the entire space appear hazy and layered. Distant light spots create circular bokeh, further enhancing the dreamlike feeling brought by shallow depth of field. The overall image presents a tranquil, contemplative everyday moment, as if capturing a moment of a girl seeking resonance in the world of music. It has a strong documentary photography style, like a real scene shot with an amateur camera, preserving film-like graininess and natural color distortion. Instead of deliberately pursuing perfection, it instead emphasizes authenticity and warmth. This non-commercial visual language makes the images more storytelling and immersive. It brings to mind those days of lingering in music stores from youth, filled with tenderness and poetry that have accumulated over time",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
          "is_user_plan": false,
          "created_at": "2026-09-17T13:54:20.693554",
