          "id": "krea2-c4350d094f89a957ad294c92",
          "alias": "单女棕外套车厢忧伤站立出神",
          "prompt": "She stands at the edge of a dimly lit subway or train platform, wearing a thick brown wool coat and a light gray wool scarf around her neck. The scarf is soft and fluffy, with fine tassels naturally hanging at the edges. Her expression is calm yet slightly melancholic, as if lost in thought or waiting for something. Light streams in diagonally from the upper left of the frame, forming a bright beam that passes through the fine dust in the air, creating a dreamy halo effect. In the foreground, the vertical lines of blurred glass windows or guardrails appear slightly blurred and light spots. The middle shot is the main subject, positioned slightly toward the center on the right side of the frame. The body is slightly turned to the side, and the head turns to the left, forming a visual guide. The background is a blurred platform environment, where distant lights, track contours, and faint train carriage outlines can be seen, but all are deeply blurred to create a strong sense of depth. The composition uses the rule of thirds, with the figure occupying the right third of the frame, leaving a large negative space for the left side to extend the light, shadow, and line of sight. The overall composition has the texture of film photography, with a cool-toned color scheme of gray, brown, Off-white is the main tone, with a retro graininess and slight fading effect. The contrast between light and shadow is strong, with bright and warm highlights and deep shadows, creating a layered interplay of light and shadow. The atmosphere is quiet and distant, full of the loneliness and poetry of urban life, as if capturing a moment of tranquility in a hurried world. The lens is 35mm prime to simulate real camera shooting, with slightly underexposed exposure enhancing the hazy feel. The background is completely out of focus, creating beautiful bokeh. The overall style is similar to the Japanese film The tranquil moments in 'Tokyo Story,' or the everyday moments captured by film photographers, show no obvious post-processing traces, preserving the original light and shadow transitions and color transitions, presenting an unretouched, authentic beauty, like those captured with an old-fashioned film camera, full of storytelling and emotional tension",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
