        {
          "id": "krea2-74a269fd9e4b2433e446233e",
          "alias": "单女米连衣裙镜前困倦站立持镜",
          "prompt": "A woman stands in a blooming field of pink flowers, her head slightly lowered. The irregular and cracked edges of the lens create an atmosphere of self-reflection and inner exploration. She wears a light beige lace slip dress with slender straps, the fabric light and breathable, gently swaying in the breeze. Her right hand gently holds the damaged mirror, fingers long and natural. In the foreground, blurred pink flowers and green stems and leaves create a soft bokeh effect. In the middle is the female subject and the mirror in her hand. The background features towering flower stems and a blue sky with white clouds. The flowers are pale pink and white, with slender stems rising upward and reaching the top of the canvas. The sky is a clear blue dotted with a few thin clouds. Light pours down from above and sides, creating a warm backlight effect. Sunlight penetrates the petals and leaves, with the overall color scheme mainly warm yellow, pink, and blue, creating a dreamy and tranquil spring atmosphere. The composition uses close-ups, with the figure positioned on the right side of the frame, leaving space on the left to extend the view to the flower sea and sky. The broken mirror serves as a visual focal point, guiding viewers to focus on the inner world of the characters. The lens uses a large aperture to blur the background and highlight the subject, simulating the realism of amateur camera or mobile phone shooting. It emphasizes natural light and authentic texture. The image has the graininess and color layers of film photography, and the overall style combines artistry with everyday elements, as if captured by a photographer on a spring afternoon using portable devices, full of poetry and philosophical reflection",
          "description": "",
          "image": "",
          "tags": [],
          "favorite": false,
          "template": false,
          "is_user_plan": false,
          "created_at": "2026-09-17T13:54:20.693554",
