        {
          "id": "krea2-04fb4f328f63fac8267077eb",
          "alias": "单女白睡裙卧室专注躺阅读",
          "prompt": "A woman lies on her side on a soft white sheet, wearing a loose white pleated nightgown with delicate ruffled designs at the collar and cuffs, presenting a lazy yet comfortable homely vibe, adding a touch of casualness and authenticity. Her posture is relaxed, her body slightly leaned back, head resting on a pillow, the pages slightly open, and the cover clearly reads \"The Pickwick Papers by Charles Dickens.\" She gently supports the book with her right hand, Her left hand naturally rests on the edge of the page, her movements smooth and natural, as if immersed in a world of reading. The entire composition centers on the character, creating a quiet and focused atmosphere. The middle frame shows her upper body and the book in her hand, occupying the upper right corner of the image. Its content and details add cultural atmosphere and a sense of life to the scene. The background is a warm indoor environment, with soft brown walls and blurred furniture outlines forming a quiet bedroom space. Light streams in diagonally from the left side of the image. This forms a bright beam of light, with rich layers of light and shadow, and delicate transitions in the shadows, creating a tranquil atmosphere in the early morning or evening. The composition combines close-ups with tilted angles, with the figure occupying most of the left side of the frame, and the gaze turning upward to the right, creating a natural visual flow. The overall image presents a subtle beauty from everyday life, like a realistic moment casually captured with an old film camera. The lens has a slight graininess and warm color tones. It enhances the sense of nostalgia and warmth. The overall color palette of the painting is mainly warm yellow and off-white, paired with soft shadows and natural light and shadow changes, creating a comfortable, peaceful, and poetic atmosphere. It feels as if time has stood still at this moment, accompanied only by the rustling of pages and the faint birdsong outside the window accompanying this quiet reading moment",
