        {
          "id": "krea2-38643e0265198815dc4c5237",
          "alias": "单女街道忧伤站立过肩",
          "prompt": "A woman stands beside a white pillar at a city street corner, wearing a dark green knitted short-sleeved top with a slightly open neckline revealing her collarbone. The tassels hang over her shoulders, fingers are slightly bent, nails neatly trimmed with light nail polish, and the background is a blurry city street. In the distance, gray building walls, metal railings, and outlines of greenery can be seen. The overall scene presents a soft, cool tone, with light diffused from a cloudy day. There are no obvious shadows, and the composition uses close-ups. The subject occupies about one-third of the left side of the frame, while the right side leaves a lot of negative space, creating a visual sense of breath. The background shows a distinct bokeh effect, and the blur treatment highlights the subject. Using a large-aperture lens with a focal length of about 85mm, it creates a strong sense of depth and intimate atmosphere. The color saturation is low but rich in layers. The overall tone is cool and has a slight grainy texture of film, making it feel like everyday moments shot with an old-fashioned film camera. The image is filled with a sense of life and a lazy sense of youth. The architectural lines and plant forms in the background are blurred into soft color blocks, enhancing the artistic and storytelling of the image. The figures' poses are naturally relaxed, as if capturing a real and intimate moment unintentionally. The entire scene exudes a quiet, gentle, and slightly melancholic urban artistic atmosphere. The transitions of light and shadow are smooth and delicate, highlights are soft and not glaring, and details in the shadows are well preserved. Overall, the image presents a serene everyday beauty. It feels as if time has frozen at this moment, allowing one to feel the innocence of youth intertwined with the sense of urban detachment. The composition is simple yet layered, and this close-up perspective brings viewers and characters psychologically, making the images more moving and immersive. The overall atmosphere is both a realistic street snapshot and a refined touch of artistic photography, as if an image was taken from a magazine or art book, full of poetry and narrative quality",
